# Converse Web Server

## Overview

The Web app (`Web,ff8`) is an optional HTTP server that gives users a browser
front-end to the BBS: browsing/downloading filebases, reading message areas, and
uploading files. It runs as a Wimp task alongside the Server and shares the
Filer databases and Support config.

Enable it with the `webserver yes` key in `<Converse$Dir>.Config.System`.

## Configuration / limits (compiled defaults)

| Setting | Default | Notes |
|---------|---------|-------|
| Listen port          | 80 | `WEB_DEFAULT_PORT` |
| Document root        | `<Converse$Dir>.Web` | `WEB_DOCROOT` - HTML templates + static assets |
| Max concurrent clients | 8 | `WEB_MAX_CLIENTS` |
| Max upload size      | 2 MB | `WEB_MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE` |
| Client timeout       | 60 s | `WEB_CLIENT_TIMEOUT` |

Activity is logged to `<Converse$Dir>.Logs.Web`.

## HTTP endpoints

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| GET  | `/`            | Index page (template) |
| POST | `/login`       | Authenticate a user; establishes a session |
| GET  | `/logout`      | End the session |
| POST | `/upload`      | Upload a file into a filebase area (<= 2 MB) |
| GET  | `/api/areas`   | JSON list of accessible file areas |
| GET  | `/download/<file>` | Download a file from a filebase |

Static files under the document root are served directly; files that contain
template tags (see below) are processed first.

## Sessions

`/login` checks the supplied credentials against the user database (the same
accounts as the BBS). On success a session is created and tracked server-side;
subsequent requests are associated with it until `/logout` or timeout. Access to
file/message areas and downloads is gated by the logged-in user's access level
and keys, exactly as on the BBS side.

## Template tags

HTML files served from the document root may contain `{{...}}` tags, expanded
per request. A file is only processed if it contains `{{`; otherwise it is served
verbatim.

| Tag | Expands to |
|-----|------------|
| `{{bbsname}}`     | The BBS name (from System config) |
| `{{username}}`    | The logged-in user's username (empty if not logged in) |
| `{{realname}}`    | The logged-in user's real name |
| `{{loggedin}}`    | Content block shown only when a user is logged in |
| `{{loggedout}}`   | Content block shown only when NOT logged in |
| `{{loginform}}`   | The login form HTML |
| `{{uploadform}}`  | The file-upload form HTML |
| `{{filebase}}`    | Rendered list of accessible file areas/files |
| `{{messagebase}}` | Rendered list of accessible message areas |

## Notes

- The server is intentionally small (single-threaded Wimp poll, capped client
  slots); it is a convenience front-end, not a general-purpose web server.
- It respects the same access control as the BBS: unauthenticated users only see
  public areas, and per-area access levels/keys apply.
